# Requests against the one-command demo (docker compose up --build).
# The IDs are the demo seed (SeedData / the InitialSchema migration): dealership Riverside, one Standard bay,
# technician Alice, the oil change (60 minutes), and the sample customer's Honda Civic.
# Times are plain local times on one clock, with no offset (ADR-0002 #25).
#
# @start must be a future Tuesday (the only day the seeded dealership and technician work, 08:00-17:00)
# within the 90-day booking horizon. 2026-11-10 is a Tuesday.
# The database volume keeps bookings between runs; docker compose down -v resets the demo data.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@start = 2026-11-10T09:00:00
@customerId = c0570000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@vehicleId = ca700000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@serviceTypeId = 5e7c0000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@dealershipId = dea10000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@unknownDealershipId = dea10000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000ff

### 1. Book an oil change at @start -> 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "requestedStart": "{{start}}"
}

### 2. The same request again -> 409 Conflict
# Today the code is NoQualifiedTechnicianAvailable, because Alice and the only bay are taken.
# It books the same vehicle again, so once rule 8 is built the code becomes VehicleAlreadyBooked.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "requestedStart": "{{start}}"
}

### 3. A dealership that does not exist -> 404 Not Found
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceTypeId}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{unknownDealershipId}}",
  "requestedStart": "{{start}}"
}
